series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md:210:**The Quieting — first encounter:** An ancient ruin site where Path abilities stop working. The Arbiters go silent within 200 meters of the site perimeter. Oryn can't access her Tide Path healing. Cael, notably, is unaffected — his Fractured Path operates normally throughout. He doesn't mention this immediately. He needs to think about what it means.
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:33:- [ ] **Book 6 delivery (the ending / Arc 3 handoff):** Chapter 24 — the companions in the edge territories for the first time, beyond the Registry Line, with no institutional backing, no ranking protection, and a Compact classification file that now reads, verbatim: ***active non-compliance, observation priority escalated.*** Cael's fragment log contains **NINE integrated abilities** by book's close. He still doesn't have a tier. The edge territories are staged as the literal handoff into Arc 3 ("The World," Books 7–9) — the door Book 7 walks through. The Quieting is NOT introduced, named, hinted, or foreshadowed — it is Book 7's first encounter and nothing in this book brushes it. Oryn remains reserved and unmet; NO Tide Path practitioner appears on-page anywhere in this book (drafting constraint carried forward from Book 5, for the same reason).
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:35:- [ ] **Book 6 delivery (Seln comes inside — the asymmetry-debt PAID):** Chapter 15. When Seln opens the cache, Cael answers in kind: the mechanism — the Book 3 SECRET — disclosed to Seln in full, the first expansion of the circle since Karis, making it six. And the debt Book 4 Ch14 filed as "no current payment mechanism" is paid on the page: Cael tells him about Shadow-adjacent — acquired during the records-office operation Seln let him watch — and about the seal: that through the tournament, through the banking's death, through a Gold-tier match he nearly lost, Shadow-adjacent stayed sealed because exposing it would have burned its source. Seln's response is one sentence and is the closest thing to being moved the series will ever show him (drafting note: keep it under ten words). The seal STAYS on publicly after this book — the logic updates (a defector's tradecraft in Cael's hands would confirm the surveillance-era acquisition) but the discipline holds.
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:122:The Vastin chapter — first beat of the book's instrument arc, staged in the limited third-person window the series reserves for him. The proceedings' evaluation architecture crosses his desk the way everything about this file has crossed his desk for three books — except this time as a courtesy copy, not a query. The window watches him read the challenge with forty years of craft and reach the same finding Karis reached in Chapter 2, faster: the corridor, the one-way doors, the re-evaluation that is not an evaluation. And the window watches what he does about it, because doing is his language: he petitions for standing to submit an evaluator's finding to the proceedings — the continent's senior-most evaluator, the only Compact official who has personally assessed the enrollee, offering the proceedings his findings under his own name.
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:249:And then the chapter's second movement, the debt paid: Cael answers the case in kind. The mechanism — the Book 3 SECRET — disclosed to Seln in full, on the page, the circle's first expansion since Karis: the integration, the fragments, the notices, the log. And Shadow-adjacent: acquired during the records-office operation Seln let him watch, sealed ever since — through the tournament, through the banking's death, through four exchanges against a Gold — because exposing it would have burned its source. Seln looks at the boy who kept his cover at Gold-tier cost, for a long moment, and the book gives him his sentence (drafting note: under ten words, no warmth performed, all of it real). The keeper and the kept, each holding the other's file for years, both files now open on the same table.
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:345:The second track: the machine's paperwork, faceless by design. The proceedings closed as moot; the re-evaluation order unexecuted against a person no longer within any enrollment; the asset-restriction inventory filed *pending jurisdiction* — the registry's grammar for a hand closing on air. Vastin's beat, the arc's last note this book: the closure summary crosses his desk as a courtesy copy, with the resignation filings appended, and the window — three sentences, no more — watches him read the five names and the personnel query on the sixth, understand the whole shape at once, as he was always going to, and return the summary to its folder unannotated. The man who wrote *continue observation* into the file three books ago writes nothing into it now. That is the entire beat, and the book intends it to land like a door.
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:377:- [ ] **Book 5 → Book 6 seam verified against Book 5's architecture close:** Book 5 ends on the road home from Norhold — Cael seventeen (B5 Ch14 on-page birthday), **seven confirmed fragments + Tide anomaly** (Storm-adjacent still flagged *stability: provisional* at B5 close — this book clears the flag explicitly in Ch1's inventory as winter-settled, so the fragment math opens clean), banking formally spent (B5 Ch19–20) with Shadow-adjacent the sole remaining seal, Halcenvane third on the continent, Brom continental Copper champion with advancement review scheduled and PENDING, Lira Iron R1 with Silver-bracket ambition declared on-page, Karis Iron R3, Seln at the table and still at his desk, Vastin still formally the Compact's instrument having testified against pre-decision at the Ch24 convening, Ilsev's second referral returned *closed — no further inquiry authorized*, Havel five note-entries deep, and the threat-classification question *entered for formal proceedings* — no vote, no ruling. Book 6 honors all of it: the ~two-month skip is explicit and staged in Chapter 1; the classification challenge is the formal output of exactly those proceedings (Ch1–2) and pre-empts nothing B5 decided, because B5 deliberately decided nothing; the Vastin relationship builds strictly from the Ch23-B5 warning baseline; the walkout stakes (Brom's review, Lira's Silver trajectory, Karis's ranking, Seln's desk) are the ones B5 built and left standing for this purpose.
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:379:- [ ] **SECRET discipline — one discharged, the rest sealed:** SERIES SECRET #2 (the Compact has been falsifying classifications for two centuries) is REVEALED this book, on schedule, per the spoiler ledger — and its reach is strictly bounded: inner circle + Seln + Vastin, seven people, no publication, no filing, no use in the proceedings (the impossibility argued on the page, Ch19). The Book 3 SECRET (the integration mechanism) expands by exactly ONE person: **Seln learns the mechanism in Ch15** — the circle's first expansion since Karis, staged as the answer to the cache and the payment of the B4 Ch14 asymmetry-debt (Shadow-adjacent's origin and its tournament-long seal disclosed to him on the page). Nobody else learns it: Ephram does not (Ch20 explicitly), Vastin does not (he receives the falsification evidence, never the mechanism — his "designed to be" line is about the system, not about Cael's architecture), Daeva still holds only the B5 shape, the public still holds only wrong theories. Book 8's Architect SECRET: untouched — the sub-layer's base stratum is aged as *older than the modification* and attributed to NO ONE (Ch16's stated limit); the Architect is not named, hinted, or approached. The Level 4 flag's TRUE ultimate source (the Architect's will, per the STATE_LEDGER's SECRET row) is not contradicted: the book's finding — the flag is the corrections function's contingency, fired from the sub-layer — is true as far as the cache can see and explicitly bounded by the cache's two-century reach; the layer beneath the layer stays dark.
books/book-07-void-roads/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:7:**Antagonist escalation: the Quieting — a phenomenon, not a person; the Compact is present only as a shape on the wrong side of a line (one off-channel reach across the Line, Chapters 17–19, faceless by design); Vastin does NOT appear in person (one courtesy-copy window, Ch16)**
books/book-07-void-roads/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:30:- [ ] **Book 7 delivery (the Quieting — first encounter, exactly per bible):** An ancient ruin site where Path abilities stop working (Ch10–11: the Fallow Ring). Arbiters go silent within two hundred meters of the site perimeter (the number is measured on the page, paced by Karis, and it is two hundred meters — the bible's figure, honored). Oryn cannot access her Tide healing inside it (Ch11, staged at the worst possible moment). **Cael is unaffected — his Fractured Path operates normally throughout.** He does not mention this immediately: he needs to think about what it means, and the book gives him the exact chapters it costs him to say it (Ch11 the fact, Ch12 the silence, Ch15 Lira, Ch16 the circle). What the Quieting IS — the Architect's preserved will priming a reset — is a SECRET with a Book 10–11 horizon and is touched by NO ONE: no character theorizes a maker, a purpose, or an intelligence. The bible's continuity rule is honored to the letter: the Quieting spreads from ancient sites outward and does not appear in cities; in this book it does not spread at all — every site is stable, old, and exactly the size it was when the locals' grandparents learned to walk around it. Expansion is Book 9's.
books/book-07-void-roads/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:37:- [ ] **B6 threads honored at their correct altitude:** *The faceless faction* — reaches across the Line exactly once (Ch17–19): a contract laid on the Lowmarch board through an edge-territory broker, priced too well, aimed at quiet ground, which Seln reads as Compact-shaped inside a day; the team that waits inside it is off-channel, nameless, and equipped for practitioners who cannot use their Paths — because the Compact *knows what quiet ground does* (plant a, above, given teeth). Still unnamed, still unlocated, still open into Book 8+. *The Compact's question about what Seln kept* — the trap is for the case as much as the boy, and Seln says so (Ch18); the case is not taken; the dread stays live. *Asset-restriction, pending jurisdiction* — the reason nobody goes west, stated once (Ch2), and the reason the trap has to come east. *Daeva's rematch / Reydan's answer* — one log line each (Ch14, Ch24), warm, unscheduled, not advanced. *Hesk* — letter beats only, via the Lowmarch courier chain (Ch4, Ch14, Ch24); his history untouched. *Vell* — one letter (Ch24). *Ephram* — one letter, from inside (Ch9), the inside friend reporting the weather. *Vastin* — one window (Ch16), three sentences, still inside, receiving a courtesy copy and writing nothing; his departure and the classified-history material are Book 8's and are not staged, hinted, or scheduled. *Havel, Ilsev, Withrow, Coss* — offstage entirely.
books/book-07-void-roads/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:53:**Tide Path (new Path defined this book — PROVISIONAL; consistent with B2's "Tide-adjacent" anomaly label and the bible's Book 15 "Oryn's Tide Path burns out"):** Flow architecture. Where Ember declares ignition and Iron Skin declares density, Tide declares *current*: the perception and redirection of internal energy flow — a practitioner's own and, at contact, another's. Its civil face is healing: restoring flow to damaged architecture so the body can do the rest. Its diagnostic technique is **the reading** — contact, both hands, the healer's own current run *through* the patient's architecture to feel where it pools, breaks, or runs wrong; Oryn describes it as "listening with my hands to how you're built." Limitations, weaknesses, costs (charter §1.2, stated before second use): contact range only, always; healing spends the healer's own reserve at roughly the rate of the damage repaired — Oryn cannot heal a crowd and cannot heal herself; the reading takes minutes, not seconds, and the patient must be still; a Tide practitioner **cannot heal what she cannot read** — architecture that returns no legible current is architecture she cannot touch, which is why Cael's injuries have always healed on their own schedule under every healer he ever saw, and why she stays. Combat use exists and is rare: at contact, a Tide practitioner can *stall* another's current for a breath — a hand on a wrist and the declaration doesn't render — at brutal cost to her own reserve. Oryn has done it three times in her life and hates it. Inside quiet ground: nothing. She is a woman with a good kit and strong hands.
books/book-07-void-roads/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:210:The choreography is staged as a retreat with a geometry, exchange by exchange, the line as the objective: **First:** the pack's cut — the dog that takes the road is between them and the perimeter, because stillhounds den inside quiet ground for exactly this — and Seln, Pathless, is still the best positional mind in the country and calls the lane that isn't cut. **Second:** Brom takes the rear with a carter's crossbow and his body, and the chapter stages what an Iron Skin practitioner is without Iron Skin: a big man with good footwork and a bolt, holding a lip of fused stone against animals that can smell nothing on him, which is the fight's cruelty and its gift — silent bodies are nearly invisible to them, and the pack hunts by *sound* now, and the unit is quiet by four books of training. **Third:** Lira, on the ankle that has now gone three times, runs the lip with a knife and the not-holding-back style stripped to bone, and the chapter's first cost lands: a hound gets her forearm and does not let go, and she cannot burst it off, and Brom's bolt takes it through the eye at four meters. **Fourth — the turn:** sixty meters from the line, Karis goes down — a hound under her, her hands on its throat, no lattice to light — and the pack converges on the noise, and the unit is not going to reach her before the pack does. Cael, who has held nine fragments to nothing for eleven chapters on ground where nothing should work, stops holding. Wind-adjacent, full, loud — the loudest thing in the Quiet — *toward* the pack, not away, the ford's trick inverted: he is the declaration, he is the only one on this floor that can make one, and every hound turns to him. Then Compression-adjacent to take the first two at contact. Then Ember-adjacent, one ignition point on fused stone, which does something to the pack Karis will spend a chapter on: they *break*, not away from him but *out* — past the line, into the scrub, gone. The chapter does not explain it. It notes that on ground where nothing works, one thing worked, and the animals that live there had never met it.
books/book-07-void-roads/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:212:The line, reached. Oryn is not with them; the book is honest that this is the chapter that needed her, and she is nine days north on her route. Costs, ledgered on the page: Lira's forearm bitten through, bleeding hard, the ankle gone for good this season; Karis's throat bruised and her voice gone; Brom's bolt-hand cut open on the crossbow's string; Seln unmarked, which from Seln is a whole report; Cael — the first full-suite deployment since the Daeva match, on top of ribs three weeks healed — spent to the ground and catalogued as such. And the chapter's last cost, unspoken: everyone saw. Five practitioners with no Paths watched the sixth use his, inside the Quiet, and saved them with it, and nobody says anything, because the priority is Lira's arm.
books/book-07-void-roads/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:288:*The Vastin window, one paragraph, the book's only, three sentences:* a courtesy copy — an edge-territory broker's completed-contract report, forwarded through a registry office that should have no interest in Lowmarch's board — crosses his desk, marked *Fallow Ring: crew returned, instruments not recovered*. He reads the site name, and the window watches a forty-year evaluator recognize a designation from a classified index he has never had cause to open, and return the copy to its folder unannotated. Still inside. Writing nothing. Book 8's.
books/book-07-void-roads/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:303:The contract: a second quiet-ground posting, from the same broker, for the same "instruments," at a second site — the Long Stair, a day south — priced at three times the first. Seln reads it and the chapter gives him the professional's chapter-within-a-chapter: registry prose again; the same broker, who Pike says has posted nothing else in a year; a price that is not an incentive but a *lure*, sized for a crew that went in once and came out; and a site chosen where the poster knows — because the poster stamped the stakes — that six practitioners will be five bodies and one anomaly. "This isn't a contract," he says. "It's a pre-restriction inventory. They've mapped what we do inside, and they've priced a floor where we can't do it." Karis: "They don't know about Cael." Seln: "They don't need to. They want the case. The boy's the price of the case." The Compact's question about what he kept — B6's open dread — has crossed the Line wearing a broker's seal.
books/book-07-void-roads/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:414:- [ ] **Book 6 → Book 7 seam verified against Book 6's ARCHITECTURE close (Book 6 prose is in progress on a separate machine at the time of drafting — RE-VERIFY THIS SEAM AGAINST DRAFTED B6 CH23–24 PROSE BEFORE ANY BOOK 7 CHAPTER IS DRAFTED, per the B3→B4 precedent):** Book 6 ends at the first edge-territory camp beyond the Registry Line — Cael eighteen (B6 Ch14 on-page birthday), **nine confirmed fragments + Tide anomaly** (Anchor-adjacent B6 Ch13 and Blade-adjacent B6 Ch20 both integrated; Storm stability flag cleared B6 Ch1), banking spent (B5) with Shadow-adjacent's *public* seal still logically in force (out here there is no public — the seal is moot beyond the Line and the book says nothing about it; Shadow-adjacent is used freely inside quiet ground and on the void roads, which is consistent: no registry, no cover to burn), Lira Iron R1 formal / Silver trajectory declined, Brom Copper formal forever / continental champion, Karis ranking forfeited / three boxes, Seln defected in form / cache traveling with them, the Compact file reading *active non-compliance, observation priority escalated*, asset-restriction *pending jurisdiction*, Vastin inside and writing nothing, Ephram at Halcenvane, Withrow's ledger banked, the faceless faction unnamed, the nameless operative's account "unpayable," Daeva's rematch "relocated," Hesk's satchel in hand. Book 7 honors all of it: the ~six-week skip is explicit and staged in Ch1; nobody goes west and the reason is stated once (Ch2); the cache is never opened and is what the trap is for (Ch17–19); the three boxes are load-bearing (Ch6 — the cart) and become the field archive; Vastin's single window (Ch16) is three sentences, courtesy-copy, unannotated, and stages nothing of Book 8's departure; Ephram writes once (Ch9).
books/book-07-void-roads/CHAPTER_ARCHITECTURE.md:425:- [ ] **PROVISIONAL facts used:** Tide Path and its mechanics (current, the reading, the stall, the cost arithmetic, "cannot heal what she cannot read") — PROVISIONAL, defined this book; Books 8–15 must match, and Book 15's "Oryn's Tide Path burns out" should be built on the reserve-cost mechanics established here. The Quieting's observable mechanics (sharp boundary, perfect circle, ~200 m radius, identical Arbiter failure, fused-stone floors, carvings, fauna denning) — PROVISIONAL, consistent with the bible's LOCKED description and SECRET source; Book 8+ must keep the mechanics and may extend them (the fourth site's doubled radius is the deliberate extension hook). The edge territories' institutions (Lowmarch, the board, the ledger, the holds, the route, the courier chain) — PROVISIONAL worldbuilding built to the series' text-over-custom / ledger-over-tier doctrine. The fauna — PROVISIONAL; stillhounds' Path-sense and the shale-backs' flight response are the two rules fights depend on and are taught before use. Pike, Ghent, the broker, the off-channel team's provenance — PROVISIONAL, new, deliberately under-explained. The Compact's survey/cordon activity (five to six years old by the stakes) — PROVISIONAL in detail, consistent with the bible's Book 8 "suppressing the Quieting data for six years."

